# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Project Overview

**UIGen** is an AI-powered React component generator. Users describe components in a chat, and Claude generates React code in real-time, displayed in a live preview. The app uses a virtual file system abstraction (no disk writes), persists projects to SQLite, and integrates with Anthropic's Claude API (or a mock provider for demos).

## Quick Commands

```bash
# Setup (install deps, generate Prisma, run migrations)
npm run setup

# Development (runs on port 3000, or next available if in use)
npm run dev
npm run dev:daemon     # Daemon mode, logs to logs.txt

# Build & Deploy
npm build
npm start

# Testing
npm test               # Run all tests (Vitest + jsdom)
npm test -- <file>    # Run single test file

# Code quality
npm run lint

# Database
npx prisma studio    # Open Prisma Studio GUI
npx prisma migrate dev --name <name>  # Create new migration
npm run db:reset      # Wipe and reinit database
```

## Architecture

### High-Level Flow

1. **Pages & Layout** (`src/app/`)
   - `/` — Home page (auth check, redirects to most recent project or anonymous mode)
   - `/[projectId]` — Project page (fetch project data, pass to MainContent)
   - `main-content.tsx` — Main UI container; manages Preview/Code tabs and splits layout

2. **Chat & Generation** (`src/app/api/chat/route.ts`)
   - POST endpoint that receives user messages + file state
   - Calls Vercel AI SDK's `streamText()` with Claude (Anthropic) or mock provider
   - Tools: `str_replace_editor` (edit file content), `file_manager` (create/delete/rename)
   - Streams response back; on finish, saves project to DB if authenticated

3. **Virtual File System** (`src/lib/file-system.ts`)
   - `VirtualFileSystem` class: in-memory tree structure for component files
   - Methods: `createFile`, `readFile`, `deleteFile`, `renameFile`, `getAllFiles`
   - Serializes to/from plain objects for DB storage and React context
   - Used by chat route and UI to stay in sync

4. **React Contexts** (`src/lib/contexts/`)
   - **FileSystemContext** — holds VirtualFileSystem instance, selected file, refresh trigger
   - **ChatContext** — holds chat messages, project ID, handles message streaming

5. **Components** (`src/components/`)
   - `chat/ChatInterface` — Message list + input, handles streaming
   - `chat/MarkdownRenderer` — Renders markdown with syntax highlighting
   - `editor/CodeEditor` — Monaco editor for browsing/editing generated code
   - `editor/FileTree` — Directory tree sidebar
   - `preview/PreviewFrame` — Live iframe that renders component via @babel/standalone
   - `auth/` — Sign in / Sign up forms, JWT token exchange

6. **Data & Auth**
   - **Prisma** (SQLite) — User (email, password hash) and Project (messages, file data as JSON)
   - **Auth** (`src/lib/auth.ts`) — JWT token in httpOnly cookie, 7-day expiry
   - **Middleware** (`src/middleware.ts`) — Session verification

### Key Design Decisions

**Virtual File System over Disk:**
- All generated code stays in memory or serialized in DB; no file writes to disk
- Keeps project state portable and isolated
- Serializes to simple object format for storage/transmission

**Mock Provider Fallback:**
- If `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is not set, `MockLanguageModel` returns canned demo responses
- Lets users demo the UI without needing a real API key
- Mock generates tool calls to show the interaction pattern

**Component Generation via Tool Use:**
- Claude doesn't generate code as plain text; instead uses `str_replace_editor` and `file_manager` tools
- Allows Claude to iteratively refine files, create new ones, see tool feedback
- `maxSteps` reduced for mock (4 steps) vs. real Claude (40 steps) to avoid repetitive loops

**Streaming UI Updates:**
- `streamText()` from Vercel AI yields text-deltas and tool-calls in real-time
- Client receives stream, updates chat messages and file system as stream progresses
- Gives impression of live code generation

## File Organization

```
src/
├── app/                           # Next.js App Router pages
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   ├── page.tsx                   # Home / auth redirect
│   ├── [projectId]/page.tsx       # Project view
│   ├── main-content.tsx           # Layout & tabs logic
│   └── api/chat/route.ts          # Chat streaming endpoint
├── components/                    # React components
│   ├── auth/                      # Sign in/up forms
│   ├── chat/                      # Chat UI, message list
│   ├── editor/                    # Code editor, file tree
│   ├── preview/                   # Preview iframe
│   └── ui/                        # Radix UI primitives
├── lib/                           # Core logic
│   ├── contexts/                  # React contexts (chat, file system)
│   ├── tools/                     # AI tool definitions (str_replace, file_manager)
│   ├── transform/                 # JSX transpilation utils
│   ├── file-system.ts             # Virtual file system class
│   ├── auth.ts                    # JWT session management
│   ├── provider.ts                # LLM provider (Anthropic or mock)
│   ├── prisma.ts                  # Prisma client singleton
│   └── prompts/                   # System prompts for Claude
├── actions/                       # Server actions for auth, project CRUD
├── hooks/                         # React hooks (e.g., useAuth)
└── middleware.ts                  # Next.js middleware

prisma/
├── schema.prisma                  # User & Project models
└── migrations/                    # DB version history
```

## Important Patterns

### Adding a New Feature

1. **Server-side logic**: Server action in `src/actions/` or API route in `src/app/api/`
2. **Context state**: Add to ChatContext or FileSystemContext if it's shared UI state
3. **UI**: React component in `src/components/`, use context hooks
4. **Tests**: Colocate tests in `__tests__/` folder next to component

### Modifying the Generation Prompt

- System prompt is in `src/lib/prompts/generation.tsx`
- Sent with every chat request (with `cacheControl: ephemeral` for prompt caching)
- Include tool definitions here if adding new tools

### Adding a New Tool

1. Define tool in `src/lib/tools/<name>.ts` (export a `build<Name>Tool` function)
2. Add to `tools` object in `src/app/api/chat/route.ts`
3. Update generation prompt with tool description
4. Tool receives VirtualFileSystem instance, can modify files

### Testing

- **Unit tests**: Vitest + @testing-library
- **File**: `__tests__/<component>.test.tsx` next to component
- **jsdom environment**: Configured in `vitest.config.mts`
- Run: `npm test -- --run` (single run) or `npm test` (watch mode)

## Database

**Models:**
- `User`: id (CUID), email (unique), password (bcrypt hash), createdAt, updatedAt
- `Project`: id (CUID), name, userId (optional for anon projects), messages (JSON string), data (JSON string), createdAt, updatedAt

**Migrations:**
- Located in `prisma/migrations/`
- Run on startup via `npm run setup`
- To add a migration: `npx prisma migrate dev --name <description>`
- To reset: `npm run db:reset` (deletes data; only for dev)

## Environment Variables

```
JWT_SECRET=<secret-key>                    # For JWT signing (required in production)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...               # Optional; if not set, uses mock provider
NODE_ENV=development|production            # Defaults to development
```

## Known Issues & Warnings

1. **`npm audit fix` is not recommended** — dependencies are pinned for compatibility; audit fix may break the app
2. **next.config.ts turbopack warning** — `root` option may not be recognized in some Next.js versions; safe to ignore
3. **Port 3000 in use** — dev server auto-selects next available port (e.g., 3002)
4. **Mock provider repetition** — `maxSteps` is lower (4) for mock to avoid lengthy loops; real Claude uses 40 steps

## Debugging Tips

- **Check streaming errors**: Look at browser console and server logs for streaming failures
- **File system sync issues**: Compare FileSystemContext state with chat messages in Redux/DevTools
- **Auth redirects**: Verify JWT is being set/read correctly in `src/lib/auth.ts`
- **Preview rendering fails**: Check if component has syntax errors; Babel transpiler will fail silently if JSX is invalid
- **Database issues**: Run `npx prisma studio` to inspect current state, or `npm run db:reset` to start fresh
